{"duration_api_ms":26748,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"feab270b-eb37-480a-8853-c33eab04674b","total_cost_usd":0.0364374,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":35298,"output_tokens":1265,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":986},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":9,"output_tokens":1265,"cache_read_input_tokens":35298,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6776,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006846,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-4-5":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":1265,"cacheReadInputTokens":35298,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.029591400000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":986,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Looking at the provided material:\n\n## 1. What guarantee does the API make about an article's slug?\n\nThe navigation map explicitly states that `Article.slug is unique` in the Prisma schema. The test suite confirms slugs are used as stable identifiers for retrieval, update, and deletion operations.\n\n## 2. How does an article or profile response reflect the REQUESTING user's relationship to the author (following, favorited), including for anonymous/unauthenticated requests?\n\nArticle responses include a `favorited` boolean (whether the requester favorited it), and profile responses include a `following` boolean (whether the requester follows that user). For unauthenticated requests, these flags default to `false` (as shown in the profile test: \"should get profile without auth\" expects `following: false`).\n\n## 3. What makes an incoming request authenticated, and what happens when the token is missing or invalid?\n\nRequests are authenticated via an `Authorization: Token <jwt>` header (the navigation map references JWT sign/verify utilities and auth middleware). When the token is missing or invalid, the API returns **401 Unauthorized** (confirmed across multiple test cases for protected endpoints like POST /api/articles, GET /api/user, etc.).","ttft_ms":20978,"type":"result","duration_ms":25730,"uuid":"ab35259a-aa62-4e17-a567-8f52c927913e","ttft_stream_ms":1884,"time_to_request_ms":30,"first_content_frame_ms":2401,"queued_turn_count":0}
